WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.680
It took quite a while for my dream to be realized,

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.260
but now it’s finally within my grasp.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.720
Even if my head and my heart disagree,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:16.450
they are beginning to come together as one.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.920
With the meetings and reunions,
this is the beginning of it all.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.500
But for everyone, this is just a small stepping stone along their lives’ paths.

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.340
The troops will gather soon,
and new bonds will be forged.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:39.610
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.080
This room is finally fit for a commanding officer, isn’t it?

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:47.550
That’s true.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:51.150
It’s a good thing we were able to find a desk that’s your size, Rein.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:54.890
It totes fits me!

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.130
Yes, come in!

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.770
Excuse us.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:02.720
So you’ve finished changing into your new uniforms!

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:04.610
You two look fabulous!

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.580
Thanks, Rein.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.280
The three of us haven’t been
in the same uniform since junior high, right?

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:15.500
It really brings back memories.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:19.250
Anyway, seeing as you’ll be flying or running around so much, Nanoha,

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.970
you might end up spending more time in your instructor’s uniform.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:27.140
Well, I’ll be wearing this while performing official duties and during ceremonies as well.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.840
Well then, it’s about time.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:31.720
Indeed.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.060
From today onwards,

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.810
Captain Nanoha Takamachi.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.490
Enforcer Fate Testarossa-Harlaown.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:44.230
The two of us will hereby be stationed at Riot Force 6.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.410
It’s a pleasure to be working under your command.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.370
Okay. I’ll be counting on you!

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:54.270
Please enter.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.110
Excuse me.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:02.840
Captain Takamachi,
Enforcer Testarossa-Harlaown,

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.820
it’s a pleasure to see you again!

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.220
Could you be Griffith?

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.640
Yes, ma’am. Griffith Lowran.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.560
It’s been so long! But that aside,
it’s amazing! You’ve really grown!

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:21.250
Yeah. Last time we met, he was only this tall.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.110
I-I’m grateful I was under the care of you two back then.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.690
Have you joined this unit too, Griffith?

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:27.110
Yes, ma’am.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:30.400
He’s my adjutant, in charge of logistics.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.110
He also helps manage relations with our superiors.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:37.080
Is your mother, Admiral Laty, doing well?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.280
Yes. Thank you for your concern!

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:42.010
Oh! May I report to you first?

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:43.720
Go ahead.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:49.040
The four forwards, as well as
the staff of Riot Force 6, have all arrived.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.840
At the moment, they are standing by in the lobby.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.140
Really? That was rather fast.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:59.520
In that case, Nanoha, Fate,
let’s greet everyone in the unit.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:26.970
I’m Riot Force 6’s director, this unit’s commanding officer, Hayate Yagami.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:35.100
As a unit of the Time-Space Administrative Bureau,
the protectors of peace and law,

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:42.020
it is our mission and responsibility to take on many cases to protect the people we serve.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.480
With our team of instructors with excellent achievements and strengths,

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:48.450
our young but promising forwards,

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:54.370
and our talented mechanics and support staff,

00:05:54.370 --> 00:06:00.330
I believe that everyone can work together and overcome any and all obstacles.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.480
Well, since I don’t like long speeches,

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.290
that is all for now.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:08.980
I’m Hayate Yagami, director of Riot Force 6
and your commanding officer.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.010
Signum, it’s really been a while.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.980
Indeed, Testarossa.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.730
We haven’t met in person for half a year.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:28.180
Right. And this is the first time both of us are in the same unit.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.060
Please look after me.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:35.440
I’m the one who should be saying that.
After all, you are my immediate superior.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:39.370
That again. I haven’t gotten used to that yet.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.160
Our relationship is one of a superior and subordinate now.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:45.290
It would be poor form if I called you <i>Testarossa</i> or called out “Hey, you!”

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:47.050
Or shall I address you as “ma’am”, instead?

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.250
Please stop making fun of me like that.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.970
It’s okay if you call me <i>Testarossa</i> or just “you.”

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.930
I’ll do just that.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.600
By the way, have all of you introduced yourselves to each other yet?

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.690
We know each other’s names,
experience, and abilities.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:09.030
We also know each other’s squads and callsigns.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:12.990
I see. Then, I would like to begin your training. Is that all right?

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.410
Yes, ma’am!

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:23.040
Vice!

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.540
Is everything prepared?

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.080
Everything’s a-okay!

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:27.530
We can take off anytime.

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.970
Isn’t this helicopter one of the newer models?

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:37.390
The JF704... this model was introduced to
the Armed Services only last year. You bet it’s new.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:41.340
Its mobility and load capacity are second to none!

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:46.460
For a pilot, flying a baby like this is the ultimate joy!

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.380
Geez, Sergeant Vice!

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.520
Sergeant Vice, when you are a pilot, everyone’s lives are in your hands!

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.740
You can’t be goofy about this!

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:59.700
Yeah, yeah! I’m well aware of that, Command Sergeant Major Rein.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:08.250
Commander Yagami, Fate, where are we heading?

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.800
The capital city, Cranagan.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.670
To the Central Command Center.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:12.940
Roger!

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:14.840
Let’s go, Storm Raider.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:15.880
Okay.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.500
Take off, standby.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.260
Nanoha!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.010
Shari!

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:47.540
In the Devices I just returned to you
are chips used to record data.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.540
So be a little careful when you use them, okay?

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:53.630
And also, our mechanic, Shari, would like a word with you.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:58.350
I’m the mechanical designer
and head of communications for Riot Force 6,

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.410
Specialist Shario Finieno.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:04.580
Everyone calls me Shari, so feel free to do the same.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.100
I will be in charge of modifying and adjusting everyone’s Devices,

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:11.510
so every now and then, I’ll be observing your training.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.020
If you have any questions concerning your Devices, don’t hesitate to ask me.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:16.990
Yes, ma’am!

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.950
Well then, shall we start this training session?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.620
Sure...

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.370
But we’re going to train <i>here?</i>

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.330
Shari?

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.390
Okay!

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:31.830
This training space is Riot Force 6’s pride and joy.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:35.760
It’s a battle and area simulator that was made so Nanoha can observe your training.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.350
Stage set!

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.560
Amazing!

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.490
Vita. So this is where you were.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:09:59.450
Signum.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.080
So the new recruits have already started their training.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.360
Yup.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:07.180
You’re not going to participate?

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.330
The four of them are still hatchlings learning to walk.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.870
It’ll be a while before I help with instructing them.

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:15.760
I see.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:19.220
Anyway, I want to make use of this time to train myself.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.820
We’re in the same unit after all.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:25.160
I have to be able to protect Nanoha in the sky.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.060
I’ll leave that to you.

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:31.470
Oh yeah, where’s Shamal?

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:33.040
In her fortress.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.940
This is a great clinic.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.910
With this, I should be able to perform pretty good check-ups and healing.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:43.570
Though the equipment we’re using was discarded by the hospital at the Main Office,

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:46.320
there shouldn’t be any problems with them whatsoever!

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:50.850
Everyone’s healing and check-ups are in your hands, Dr. Shamal!

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.230
Okay!

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:01.080
All right, can everyone hear me?

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:01.640
Yes, ma’am!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.590
’Kay, let’s deploy the targets.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:07.100
First, we’ll warm up with a set of eight.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:11.720
How do movement level C and attack level D sound?

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:12.420
Sounds good.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:18.260
Our job is to search for, protect, and escort the Lost Logia.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:22.660
In order to complete our mission,
we’ll have to fight our enemies who are...

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.220
...these!

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:28.490
Autonomic magical machines.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:31.480
This type of enemy will attack when you approach.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:33.330
Their attacks are pretty painful!

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:36.960
And so, it’s Mock Battle Training Number One.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.230
Mission objective:

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.460
Destroy or capture the eight escaping targets.

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:43.040
You have fifteen minutes.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:43.760
Yes, ma’am!

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:44.740
Now then,

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.030
Mission...

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.800
...start!

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.400
Regarding the search for

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:06.150
antiquities known as Lost Logia,

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:09.330
I’m sure everyone already knows about them.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:13.150
The advanced technologies crafted by various ancient civilizations,

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:16.780
which have been discovered on once highly-advanced, derelict worlds,

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:21.210
are extremely dangerous artifacts.

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:26.720
Lost Logia require immediate attention,
as they are capable of

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:30.050
causing large-scale destruction and devastation.

00:12:30.050 --> 00:12:34.810
However, it has been confirmed that some of these critical items have gone missing.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:42.350
Now then, one of the main reasons we’ve requested the formation of Riot Force 6

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:46.520
was to search for these first-class Lost Logia, codenamed “Relics”.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:50.150
Relics look like any other gem on the outside,

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.990
but research tells us that they were created by an ancient civilization.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:55.980
Though we’ve yet to find out what their purpose is,

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:58.620
they have an extremely high crystalline energy capacity.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.230
Relics have been discovered four times in the past.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:05.630
On three of these occasions,
they caused great devastation to the surrounding areas.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:10.500
Also, from investigating two of the incidents,

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:13.640
we have discovered these...

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:18.940
Extremely advanced magical energy R&D facilities.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:23.270
They have all been discovered on undeveloped worlds.

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:27.980
Such research is prohibited within these sectors,

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:31.500
and the debris we found suggests they were trying to erase the evidence.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.100
They appear to be up to no good.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:37.830
At the very least,
they do not intend to benefit the public.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:42.160
Someone is gathering Relics so they can use them for their own benefit.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:45.340
The chance of rhem committing a dimensional crime is high.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:50.760
And also, this someone is using highly dangerous magical machines to find them.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.370
They are called Gadget Drones.

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:55.350
Since the discovery of the Relics,

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:59.420
they’ve searched for specific Lost Logia signatures and have tried to retrieve them.

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:02.750
They are self-powered, autonomic machines.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:20.250
What the hell? They move too fast!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.440
It’s no use... they dodged all my attacks!
I can’t hit them!

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.180
You two up front, you’re all over the place!

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:45.100
Think a little about what you’ll do next!

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:45.900
O-Okay!

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.440
Sorry!

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.800
Kid, could you give me a magical boost?

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:51.600
Okay.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:52.990
Kerykeion!

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.680
Boost Up: Barret Power

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:02.270
Shoot!

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:10.040
A barrier?

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:12.180
That’s not it... it’s a field!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.940
The magic was dispelled?

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:14.840
That’s right.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.420
The Gadget Drones have a troublesome special feature.

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:20.300
They can dispel any magic that enters

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:23.000
their anti-magilink field, or A.M.F.

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.750
Conventional magic attacks will have no effect.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.100
Dammit!

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:27.710
Why you!

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:30.110
Subaru!

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.360
Idiot, that’s dangerous!

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.410
Furthermore, when the A.M.F. has been fully expanded,

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:50.360
flight, aerial pathways, and teleportation magic
will all be dispelled within the field.

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:51.840
Subaru, are you all right?

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.760
Somehow.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:16:02.260
Well, in practice, we tweak everyone’s Devices a little to obtain a similar result,

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:06.690
but the data is real, so the result is something very similar to the real thing.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.100
There are several ways to defeat them though.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.650
Whatever you do, carefully plan it,

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:13.920
and carefully carry it out!

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:16.420
Kid, what did you say your name was again?

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.030
I’m Caro.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:23.540
Caro, do you think you can do anything with binding magic and that tiny dragon’s ability?

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:26.460
There are a few things I’d like to try.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:28.710
I have some too.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:29.940
Subaru!

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:35.340
Okay! Erio, can you get ahead of those guys and block their escape?

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.290
Tia seems to have an idea...
we need to buy them time!

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.430
I’ll try!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.230
Everyone sure can run fast.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:48.070
It’s kind of dangerous and makes your heart race though.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.500
Can you record the data from their Devices?

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.270
I’m getting some really good recordings.

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:54.990
Their four Devices are all performing well.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:58.320
Raising Heart, I’ll need your cooperation as well.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:16:59.940
All right.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:07.260
Let’s do this, Strada!

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:09.210
<b>Cartridge Load</b>

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.720
Explosion

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:30.880
Go to the scrapyard!

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:42.140
Just as I thought, if my magic gets dispelled,
I can’t output enough strength.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.180
In that case!

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:55.300
I’ll cut off their escape.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.410
Fried.

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:57.510
<b>Blast Flare</b>

00:17:59.050 --> 00:17:59.560
Fire!

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:10.800
Please heed me, things that bind,
constricting things.

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:14.030
Now hear my call, restrain my foes with steel.

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:15.570
Summoning wrought iron!

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.380
<b>Alchemic Chain</b>

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:27.750
So summoning magic can do <i>that</i>.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:32.210
The ability to combine inorganic substances... she’s quite skillful.

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:36.250
I’m a ranged specialist.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:41.220
If I give up because my attacks have no effect on it,
there’s no point in my being here!

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:47.120
Subaru, I’ll attack from above.
Make sure you get them!

00:18:47.120 --> 00:18:47.730
Got it!

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:50.680
A magical attack?
Even though they have an A.M.F.?

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:53.710
Yes. There is an available passing method.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:19:03.310
If I put a barrier around my shot,
it should make it into the field.

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:07.360
As long as the barrier isn’t totally dispelled when it hits,

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:11.080
the shot should be able to hit the target!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:15.910
You can place a barrier around
a shot so it can break through a field,

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:18.830
but it’s usually a skill for AA rank mages.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:20.010
AA?

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:24.920
Combine

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:25.910
Combine!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:32.580
<b>Variable Shoot</b>

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:45.280
Tia!

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:47.360
Nice!

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.070
That was nice, Tia! You did it, as expected!

00:19:50.070 --> 00:19:52.230
Subaru, shut up!

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.620
Of course I’d be able to do it!

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:11.940
Hayate.

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:17.020
Vita! Is everyone eating together?

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:20.100
Yes, a lot happened today.

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.610
Hayate, have you had dinner yet?

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:25.310
I didn’t even have lunch.

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:27.410
I could eat a horse right now.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:31.490
We can’t have that.
I’ll quickly fix something for you.

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:33.420
I’ll bring some tea!

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:35.290
Thanks a lot!

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:40.760
Where’s Rein?

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.220
Here.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:48.880
As usual, that girl’s fast asleep.

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:52.760
Well, she was hard at work all day.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.480
How did everything go at Central Command?

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:09.650
Well, although we’re a new unit,
they’ve decided to give us their full support.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.360
There don’t seem to be any problems.

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:18.340
We’ve been supported by Admiral Lindy, Admiral Laty,
and Chrono—<i>Admiral</i> Chrono Harlaown.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:20.760
And also, our greatest supporter is

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:24.940
the Church of the Holy King and the leader of the Church Knights, Knight Carim.

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:27.760
In any case, no one seems to be against us.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:30.220
How’s the current situation?

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:36.620
Nanoha and the forward squads are going through some hard training through the night.

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:40.150
The newbies are probably exhausted by now.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:43.060
Well, they’re determined and pretty energetic.

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:45.400
They’ll make it through somehow.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:53.680
The support team also has no problems.
Everyone is full of vim and vigor.

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:57.860
Griffith is working as hard as ever too.

00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:59.250
There don’t seem to be any problems.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:04.250
I see. It’s been ten years since we signed up.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:09.330
After all of our hardships and hard work,
we finally have it:

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:11.430
The unit of our dreams.

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:18.380
We’ll do our best to solve this Relic case and finish what Carim entrusted us with.

00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:20.550
Let’s do our best together, okay?

00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:21.980
Yeah, I’ll work hard!

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:23.350
Of course!

00:22:23.350 --> 00:22:26.400
We guardian knights will always be with you.

00:22:32.030 --> 00:22:34.700
Something smells good.

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:37.760
You woke up because of the smell?
You’re such a glutton.

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:42.480
We’re all eating dinner now.
Rein, do you want some too?

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:44.440
I want some too!

00:22:44.450 --> 00:22:46.600
Here, wash your face.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.080
I’ll give you some of mine.

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:52.460
Vita, could you get a small plate?

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:53.260
Sure.

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:57.140
Looks yummy!

00:23:00.180 --> 00:23:02.780
What do you think of the new recruits?

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:05.390
Everyone is very energetic.
I’ve got a good vibe about them.

00:23:05.390 --> 00:23:06.760
Really?

00:23:10.190 --> 00:23:12.660
It’d be great if they can learn a lot from you.

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:14.740
I’ll train them well,

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:24.460
until those kids are able to fight down their own individual paths.

00:25:17.620 --> 00:25:19.370
To be prepared to
sortie at any time,

00:25:19.370 --> 00:25:21.940
the forward members
are continuously training.

00:25:21.940 --> 00:25:24.360
You are about to meet your partner,
who will fight with you.

00:25:24.360 --> 00:25:27.130
Your Device is only for you and is customized for your use.

00:25:33.130 --> 00:25:35.200
Take off!
